# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Construction / development only — MUST NOT reach the repository.
# Per CLAUDE.md rule 6: when you create a new development-only file, add it to
# THIS section in the same commit that creates it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/_docs/
/_scratch/
/_notes/
/.claude/
/.cursor/
/.windsurf/
/.aider*
*.local.md
TODO.local*
scratch.*
*.scratch
/tmp/
/.tmp/

# One-off schema probes. Phase 29 wrote `schema-probe.php` to read the live
# InnoDB FULLTEXT settings — `innodb_ft_min_token_size`, the stopword count,
# which columns actually carry AUTO_INCREMENT — because §8.16.2 states those
# numbers and the honest way to claim them is to measure the running server.
# The findings became tests (`SearchSchemaTest`); the probe itself is scaffolding.
/schema-probe.php
/*-probe.php

# Keycloak's test certificate and key, generated by deploy/oidc-test-setup.sh
# for the Phase 24 OIDC integration. `*.key` and `*.crt` below already cover
# the files; the directory is named here so the reason is recorded beside them
# and an empty directory does not read as an oversight.
deploy/keycloak-tls/

# OpenLDAP's test certificate and key, generated by deploy/ldap-test-setup.sh
# for the Phase 26b LDAP integration. Same reasoning as the directory above.
deploy/openldap-tls/

# Generated abuse-corpus fixtures: hostile by design, rebuilt by their builders
# (tests/Fixtures/AbuseCorpus/*/build_*.py). The builders are committed; the
# artefacts are not, so the reviewable artefact is the mutation, not the binary.
tests/Fixtures/AbuseCorpus/_generated/

